ubtracting ${a}_{3}$ from ${a}_{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{4}-{a}_{3} \\\\  & =23-18 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519564 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519564 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103251" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519564 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519564 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the common difference of an arithmetic sequence if its sixth and seventh terms are $6$ and $11$, respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519564 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "947d1f31-89e5-5a9c-9e34-33e153098c01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519564 #edb/ref 1074 "The first thing to note is that the terms are *increasing*, and therefore we expect the common difference $d$ to be *positive*.\n\nSince the two terms are consecutive, we can find the common difference by subtracting ${a}_{6}$ from ${a}_{7}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{7}-{a}_{6} \\\\  & =11-6 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519575 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519575 #edb/ref 1069 "q-214179" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519575 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519575 #edb/ref 1071 "An arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{7}=6$ and ${a}_{8}=-3.$ The common difference of this sequence is $d=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519575 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a939b213-95ee-5354-bca1-280bbeed2f43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519575 #edb/ref 1074 "The first thing to note is that the terms are *decreasing*, and therefore we expect the common difference $d$ to be *negative*.\n\nSince the two terms are consecutive, we can find the common difference by subtracting ${a}_{7}$ from ${a}_{8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{8}-{a}_{7} \\\\  & =-3-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=-9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519596 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519596 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519596 #edb/ref 1071 "An arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{20}=21.5$ and ${a}_{24}=12.5.$ What is the common difference of the sequence?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519596 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee47bebb-a1a4-5edd-a0dd-08fb92af0f27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519596 #edb/ref 1074 "The first thing to note is that the terms are *decreasing*, and therefore we expect $d$ to be *negative*.\n\nWe are given the terms\n\n$$\n{a}_{20}=21.5,\\,{a}_{24}=12.5.\n$$\n\nTo find $d,$ we apply the formula with $n=24$ and $m=20:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{n}-{a}_{m}}{n-m} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{24}-{a}_{20}}{24-20} \\\\  & =\\frac{12.5-21.5}{24-20} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{4} \\\\  & =-2.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=-2.25.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519606 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519606 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519606 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519606 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the common difference of an arithmetic sequence if its third and sixth terms are $2$ and $-22$, respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519606 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9d7919f-152a-59f4-84d8-010f7c33087a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519606 #edb/ref 1074 "The first thing to note is that the terms are *decreasing*, and therefore we expect $d$ to be *negative*.\n\nWe are given the terms\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}=2,\\,{a}_{6}=-22.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $d,$ we apply the formula with $n=6$ and $m=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{n}-{a}_{m}}{n-m} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{6}-{a}_{3}}{6-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-22)-2}{6-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24}{3} \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=-8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
